        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0736" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg652"/>

                <head>No. 309.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 10, 1886</date>.
                        (Received June 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 241.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    inclosed copy and translation of the Mexican law of foreigners and
                    naturalization, published in the Diario Oficial of 7th instant.</p>
                <p>From article 39 you will perceive that the laws which established the
                    [matriculation of foreigners have been repealed. Still, these certificates of
                    matriculation <hi rendition="#italic">may</hi> be issued.</p>
                <p>The inclosed law does not embrace all the rights and obligations of foreigners,
                    as will be seen by reference to the “Derecho Internacional Mexicano, Tercera
                    Parte,” from page 369 to 421.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. L. MORGAN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d313-a1.xml" xpointer="d313-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
